accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  corrected type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  17 removed_month 93 accessioned on  17 removed_month 93 at 13 33 clinical data   none provided                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  left   biopsy  1  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  grade removed_date  removed_date cm in diameter in microscopic section  2  focal ductal carcinoma in situ  3  atypical ductal hyperplasia  note  no vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  the margins are free of tumor  two small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are present in sections separate from the infiltrating tumor  breast  left   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  18 removed_month 94 at 08 03     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     this addendum has been deleted for this report gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a removed_date x removed_date x 3cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with localizing wire in place  an x ray accompanies this specimen  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a removed_date x 0 3cm irregularly circumscribed tan lesion within 0 2cm of the inked margin  submitted entirely in a through j with lesion in f  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   suspicious nodule  too small to freeze  o r  resident  eugene f  ruffolo  md o r  diagnosis by  eugene jerome mark  m d                                                                                  source care unit  surgical day care   acc 3 reports to  susan e briggs  m d  part a  left   report_end  , Positive.
