accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  01 aug 94 accessioned on  01 aug 94 at 12 55 clinical data  breast lesion on mammogram                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  left   biopsy  1  moderately differentiated infiltrating ductal carcinoma  grade removed_date   85   two foci  see note  2  ductal carcinoma in situ   15   cribriform and micropapillary types  see note  note  the invasive component is 1 2cm in greatest dimension  as measured from the slide  and the resection margins are free of tumor  in situ carcinoma is present adjacent to  as well as in breast tissue away from  the invasive tumor  a second  0 2cm in diameter focus of invasive carcinoma is present in breast tissue away from the large tumor  this smaller focus is surrounded by in situ carcinoma  and most probably represents a second  small  primary  there is no evidence of lymphatic invasion  hormone receptor studies will be reported by immunoperoxidase  and will be reported separately  diagnosis by  teri l  moore  md signed on  04 aug 94 at 13 00                                                                                     immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  left   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  08 aug 94 at 07 18 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  left   is a removed_date x removed_date x 2 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and accompanying mammogram  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white  firm nodule  measuring removed_date x 0 5cm with irregular borders that approach the resection margin  sections of this nodule are submitted in a through e  other suspicious regions submitted in f through j  resident  edwin s  monuki  md     intra operative diagnosis     gross diagnosis  breast left   no gross tumor identified  o r  resident  stamatina kaptain  md o r  diagnosis by  max l  goodman  m d                                                                                  source care unit  surgical day care   acc 3 reports to  herbert charles hoover jr   m d  part   left breast   report_end  , Positive.
